ue, consider implementing thread-safety:\n\n**Option 1 - Use ConcurrentBag** (Quick fix):\n```csharp\npublic static ConcurrentBag<Student> students = new ConcurrentBag<Student>(new List<Student>{...});\n```\n\n**Option 2 - Use lock mechanism**:\n```csharp\nprivate static readonly object _lock = new object();\nprivate static List<Student> _students = new List<Student>{...};\npublic static IEnumerable<Student> GetStudents() \n{\n    lock (_lock) { return _students.ToList(); }\n}\n```\n\n**Impact**: Low - May cause race conditions under high concurrent load, but this is a mock data scenario.\n\n**Effort**: Low (30 minutes)\n\n---\n\n### No Breaking Changes Detected\n\nThe analysis reviewed the following against .NET 8 breaking changes:\n\n✅ **ASP.NET Core APIs**: All APIs used (WebApplicationBuilder, MapGroup, Results) are stable in .NET 8  \n✅ **Minimal API Patterns**: Correctly implemented for .NET 8  \n✅ **Dependency Injection**: Uses standard .NET 8 DI patterns  \n✅ **JSON Serialization**: No custom JsonSerializer configuration detected  \n✅ **DateTime Handling**: Standard Guid and primitive types used  \n✅ **Entity Framework**: Not used in this project  \n\n---\n\n### Files Analyzed\n\n**Project Files**:\n- ✅ MinimalAPIProject.csproj\n- ✅ MinimalAPIProject.generated.sln\n\n**Configuration Files**:\n- ✅ appsettings.json\n- ✅ appsettings.Development.json\n- ✅ Properties/launchSettings.json\n\n**Source Files** (11 files):\n- ✅ Program.cs\n- ✅ Model/Student.cs\n- ✅ Service/IStudentService.cs\n- ✅ Service/StudentService.cs\n- ✅ Repository/IStudentRepository.cs\n- ✅ Repository/StudentRepository.cs\n- ✅ Endpoint/StudentApiEndpoints.cs\n- ✅ Dto/Request/CreateStudentRequestDto.cs\n- ✅ Dto/Request/UpdateStudentRequestDto.cs\n- ✅ Dto/Response/StudentResponseDto.cs\n- ✅ Mock-Data/StudentMock.cs\n\n---\n\n### Upgrade Readiness Assessment\n\n| Category | Status | Notes |\n|----------|--------|-------|\n| **Framework Target** | ✅ Ready | Already .NET 8.0 |\n| **Package Compatibi